From 3a9f2670d47ad20811e36182b7cfd1bc0cf49d99 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tim Carney <tim.carney@cargt.com>
Date: Fri, 5 Jun 2026 12:33:11 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] imx93-cargt: Share LPDDR4X timing files across all i.MX93
 cargt boards

All i.MX93 cargt boards (00324, 00359, 00363) use the same SoM with
identical LPDDR4X timing requirements. This consolidates DDR timing
configuration to eliminate duplication and ensure consistency.

Changes:
- Create board/cargt/imx93_common/ with shared timing files:
  * 8 timing variants (512MB/1GB/2GB @ 3200/3733 MT/s, rank1/rank2)
  * Shared CSR files for 3200/3733 MT/s
  * Common timing initialization code
  * 36 .inc files with DDR configuration data
  * Reference timing files and documentation

- Unify Kconfig options across all boards:
  * CONFIG_CARGT_IMX93_LPDDR4X_TIMING_BY_NAME
  * CONFIG_CARGT_IMX93_LPDDR4X_TIMING_BY_BOARD_ID
  * CONFIG_CARGT_IMX93_LPDDR4X_TIMING_BY_EEPROM
  * CONFIG_CARGT_IMX93_MIN_SDRAM_SIZE_MB

- Update all board spl-cargt.c files with unified timing selection:
  * Comprehensive select_dram_timing() supporting all 8 variants
  * Rank patching functions for single/dual rank configurations
  * EEPROM-based timing selection with failsafe defaults

- Update defconfigs for all three boards:
  * Use unified CONFIG_CARGT_IMX93_* options (remove board-specific)
  * Increase CONFIG_SPL_MAX_SIZE from 0x26000 to 0x27000 (+4KB)
    to accommodate EEPROM timing selection code

- Remove duplicate timing files from 00324 and 00359 boards

This resolves build failures for 00359 and enables all boards to
support the full range of DDR configurations via EEPROM.

Signed-off-by: Tim Carney <tim.carney@cargt.com>
